apple tv's foundation is an epic sci-fi  story spanning several centuries based  off the 1951 trilogy by isaac asimov the  premise is somewhat simple a brilliant  mathematician by the name of harry  selden has created a mathematical  equation that can predict the future and  this future does not look good according  to harry if humanity fails to make  drastic changes it will endure 30 000  years of war and destruction this  doesn't sit well with the current ruler  of the empire who believes harry's  claims to be treasonous and an affront  to his power this is brother day also  known as the emperor he's a member of  what is known as the genetic dynasty a  long line of clones that have held onto  power for over 400 years when one of  them gets old they pass power on to a  younger copy so at any one time there  are at least three emperors of varying  ages brother dawn brother day and  brother dusk absolute power is  consolidated through brother day they're  based off of the first emperor known as  cleon the first and this ensures the  empire is ruled by a constant and  consistent hand but this also has its  downsides at the end of episode 1 a  group of insurgents blow up the  starbridge a massive tower that  transports people from space to the  planet trant or surface planet trantor  is the empire's home planet this attack  causes a hundred million deaths and only  emboldens the emperor to take action  against harry who sees the attack as the  first of many catastrophes to befall  humanity in the upcoming age of darkness  but brother day is smart instead of  executing harry he decides to exile him  to a planet on the outer reaches known  as terminus his intention is to let him  continue his work and should harry's  predictions come true use it to further  increase his power what greater weapon  for an emperor than a formula that can  predict the future this mathematical  equation is part of what is called  psycho-history psycho-history is a  predictive model designed to forecast  the behavior  of very large populations so harry is  tasked with starting a colony on  terminus and establishing what is known  as the foundation the thinking here is  that when civilization crumbles as he  has predicted humanity will need  something to build on rather than start  from nothing they'll have a foundation a  giant encyclopedia of sorts containing  all of humanity's greatest achievements  and technologies he says that with a  successful foundation this age of  darkness can be reduced from 30 000  years to a thousand for the emperor  exiling harry is a win-win if it turns  out harry's predictions are rubbish he's  already exiled if it turns out they're  true he can use it to further bolster  his own power in episode two while on  route to terminus harry selden is killed  by his adopted son reish but unbeknownst  to the crew this is all an elaborate  plan for something far greater a plan  that will see the overthrow of the  empire and the end of its tyrannical  rule this leads us to the events of the  season's final episode which starts with  harry's casket being shot out into space  prior to his death a death orchestrated  by harry himself he took a pill  containing millions of self-replicating  molecular machines these machines broke  his body down and became one with his  casket creating what is known as the  vault the vault landed on terminus  before the settlement arrived and no one  could really examine it because of a  self-defense feature known as the null  field it's an invisible force which when  one would get close to it would make  them pass out there was one person  however who was impervious to this field  that's salvor hardin the warden of  terminus but we'll get to her in a bit  as we begin the final episode two rival  factions have arrived on terminus  bringing their centuries-long hatred of  one another to the planet these are the  anakrians and thesmans and it looks as  though all-out war is imminent if it  weren't for the arrival of harry selden  emerging from the vault it's not the  real harry selden more so a  manifestation of his consciousness and  this was all part of his plan to create  a new civilization not ruled by one  voice like the empire but of many he  goes on to say but the foundation was  never about  curating knowledge  it was about curating people but how  does he hope to manage this with these  two factions who absolutely hate each  other throughout the course of the  season the show has stressed the  importance of history how whoever writes  it can turn a villain into a hero and a  liar into a truth-teller this is what  happened centuries ago with cleon ii the  first of the genetic dynasty clones he  had these two upstart kingdoms the  anacrians and thesmans who were only  getting more powerful by joining their  two kingdoms through marriage so he  orchestrated a murder involving the  royals to make it look like one of the  kingdoms backstabbed the other and voila  he rewrote history in his favor why  fight two upstart kingdoms when you can  exploit their racial animus  and have them fight each other harry  believes that if they all join together  they can bring about the downfall of the  empire and create a new civilization  that will withstand the dark times to  come they even have their hands on the  invictus the empire's largest weapon  which went missing 700 years ago and was  deemed lost for good but this is just a  starting point back on trantor brother  day decides the fate of brother dawn who  we found out was unwillingly involved in  a plot to overthrow the empire over the  course of the season brother don fell in  love with one of his servants a gardener  by the name of azura he confided in her  that he's not like his brothers he's  colorblind and left-handed but how could  this be he's supposed to be an exact  copy this doubt led him to escape  fearing if his brothers found out about  his differences they would kill him so  he seeks refuge with azura only to be  betrayed by her she's part of a  resistance the one responsible for  genetically modifying his dna meaning  someone on the inside must have had  access to the genetic tanks in which  their bodies are made this is a plan  that was years in the making and the  only person i can think of who would  have access is their servant demerizal  this is interesting for a number of  reasons first demarzel is supposed to be  programmed never to bring harm to a  member of the genetic dynasty but on the  other hand she does have motive to bring  harm she is the last of her kind her  fellow robots were killed by the very  dynasty she has sworn to protect she is  also a devout believer in luminism a  religion which almost elected a woman by  the name of zephyr halima who is an  enemy to the empire in episodes 6-8 we  see how brother day tries to sway the  vote away from halama to someone more in  line with the emperor that's because  halima believes in something called the  primary octavo a heretic scripture that  links the soul to individual sentience  in other words because the emperor is a  copy he does not possess a soul  therefore he is incapable of change this  would put the emperor in direct conflict  with the very tenets of luminism tenants  that believe change is natural and  therefore a holy progression and  luminism has 3 trillion followers so he  can't afford to start a war with them so  to get over this hurdle brother day  embarks on the spiral a 170 kilometer  holy trek through scorching desert which  few survive it is said that those who  make it to the end are granted a vision  now here is where brother day like his  ancestors rewrites history he does make  it to the end but lies about his vision  stating that he saw a birth root a  birthrate is deeply linked to the  creation of the lumenism religion and  his vision is interpreted by the ring of  zephyrs as being a holy indication that  his soul is not one of stagnation of  course we learn later that this was all  a lie brother day received no such  vision when he reached the end of the  spiral as dimmer zell says of those who  don't receive a vision  seeing nothing  i would not wish that emptiness on  anyone thousands of years ago demerizel  completed the spiral and she herself  received a vision but we never find out  what that vision is if she is in fact  working against the empire it could have  something to do with that after all when  she suddenly kills brother dawn who was  going to be spared by brother day for  his involvement in the overthrow she  rips off her face in anguish perhaps  something she had spent several years  planning was coming undone as we learned  later in the episode the shadowmaster  informs brother day that not only  brother dawn's dna has been changed but  also his own the rebels have tainted all  the copies however brother dusk is  currently being tested so he might be  the last pure copy and it makes sense  that brother day's dna has been changed  any previous clone would have opted to  kill brother dawn but brother day was  going to spare him as dimmer zell says  about all the clones in episode 2 how  often do we choose this  you always do brother day choosing the  non-violent option indicates something  has changed with things settling down on  terminus salver hardin begins her search  for answers she's been experiencing  these visions both of a young boy and  girl but isn't sure where they're coming  from we learned that salvor was the  result of her mother being in vitro  fertilized with gail dornick's egg and  rache selden's sperm eggs and sperm  would have been stored as part of the  colony's seed program although the show  doesn't really go into much depth as to  salvor's mother's motivation here those  visions of a young boy and girl were of  her mother and father gail and reish  this revelation causes salvor to take  off in the middle of the night with her  lover hugo ship the beggar they have a  tearful goodbye and she tells them she  has a lead on where to go this ends up  being her biological mother's planet of  synax speaking of her mother gail  dornick has gone on her own crazy  journey this season she won a math  competition by solving the abraxas  conjecture a problem which hadn't been  solved in 500 years this put her in  touch with harry selden who she later be  accused of being complicit in his murder  forcing her to escape the colony ship  this would lead her to a secret ship  which was meant for race and the  discovery of harry selden's  consciousness embedded in the very  weapon that was used to kill him it's  here we learn there is a second  foundation on harry's homeworld of  helicon we never get to see what happens  on helicon as gail forces her way off  the ship tired of being lied and  manipulated to by harry she ends up  putting herself back in cryo and  traveling back to cynics a journey that  takes her 138 years there she finds her  homeworld has succumbed to rising sea  levels something that was hinted at  earlier on in the season and as she  finds her home underwater she notices a  blinking light a light which will lead  her to a pot containing her daughter  salver hardin we aren't exactly sure how  she got here or for how long but with  the foundation being renewed for season  2 we'll be sure to find out this leaves  us with three major storylines to jump  off from brother daenerysel the citizens  of foundation and gail and salvor i  thought it was quite curious when they  showed gail still had racist dagger a  dagger that contained harry selden's  consciousness so i wouldn't be surprised  if harry and gail will be reunited once  again whether it be on synax or  elsewhere but i want to hear what you  thought of this first season of  foundation was it enough to keep you  intrigued and what do you think will  happen in season 2. thanks for watching  be sure to like and subscribe and for  more bad takes you can follow me on  twitter and instagram at think story yt  until next time remember daddy loves you  very much  you

